<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89923" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσπελ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cause to approach, bring near to</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέα μέν μοι κατέαξε . . ἄκρῃ προσπελάσας</span>
			<i>having driven</i> her <i>against</i> the headland, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.285
			</span></i>: —
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσπελασθείς</span> is 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρὸς πελ</span>
			. in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1101
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν ἁφήν</span>
			<i>apply</i> touch, <i><span class="en">
				Marcellin.
				<u>Puls.</u>
				130
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>approach</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				206d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				15.42
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>associate with</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.47
			</span></i> W.; also of hostile <i>approach</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				22.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				39.6
			</span></i>; <i>deal with</i>, in argument, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).278
			</span></i>; <i>visit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς αὐτοφυέσι . . ὕδασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Trall.
					8.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
